<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="050" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-22: Invoice harness — invoice orchestration moves onto the pipeline as the second harness; invoice domain code stays; eBilling tests and E2E pass unchanged (HARD GATE: eBilling UAT sign-off)</title>
    <phase>3 Invoice harness</phase>
    <gate>after:029 + eBilling owner UAT sign-off (projects/ebilling-r1/tasks/163-uat-dev-rollout.poml)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags bff-api, worker, job; rewires a production invoice processing path (.cs) owned by another project.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Touches eBilling's hot path (`InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler`, rerun handler) and must preserve its invariants ("a linked submission is never Failed", resume-on-link hold) exactly; judgment on where the seam sits.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3-A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Single task in its group; edits shared eBilling job handlers and the harness registry.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>029</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, backend, worker, job, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>After eBilling UAT sign-off, register an invoice harness on the intake pipeline: an `IIntakeHarness` for request type Invoice that drives the existing invoice submission work (Content Understanding read, line coding, rules and holds, the invoice transaction and commit gate, tracking and resubmission numbers, reason codes, firm notices, approval lifecycle) as stages under a `sprk_processingjob` run, with `sprk_invoicesubmission` keeping the request role. The domain code stays where it is; only the orchestration moves. eBilling's existing tests and end-to-end run must pass unchanged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the eBilling submission pipeline, ADR-004 job handlers and the intake orchestrator from tasks 012–013. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>An `InvoiceIntakeHarness` registered behind a kill switch under which invoice submissions run as intake runs, with the linked-submission and resume-on-link invariants intact and eBilling's suite green with no test edits.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-22 (a–c), owner Q4 (invoices in Phase 3, only after eBilling UAT; no eBilling edits until then), success criterion 7, project CLAUDE.md §4 (ebilling-r1 owns `Services/Finance/**`). The orchestrator (013) and harness registry (`Services/Intake/Harnesses/IIntakeHarness.cs`, `IntakeHarnessRegistry.cs`, task 012) exist; the NDA harness (015) is the sibling reference. ebilling-r1 note 049 documents the submission processing job and its invariants.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/Harnesses/Invoice/InvoiceIntakeHarness.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Intake/InvoiceIntakeHarnessTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler.cs (only if the seam requires it; after sign-off)</file>
      <file role="modify">the intake DI module / harness registration created by tasks 012–013</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/Harnesses/Nda/NdaIntakeHarness.cs (task 015, harness shape)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Jobs/InvoiceSubmissionRerunJobHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/ (InvoiceSubmissionService, InvoiceSubmissionProcessor, InvoiceSubmissionPersister, InvoiceSubmissionRerun) — domain code, read first</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/049-submission-processing-job.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Jobs/Handlers/InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandlerTests.cs, InvoiceSubmissionProcessingFlowTests.cs — must pass unchanged</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="029" status="pending">Phase 1 on dev: orchestrator, run record, harness registry.</dependency>
      <dependency task="ebilling-r1/163" status="external">eBilling owner UAT sign-off.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = the whole task. HARD GATE: no edit to `Services/Finance/Submission/` (or any eBilling file) before the eBilling owner's UAT sign-off on ebilling-r1 task 163 is confirmed in chat (FR-22 c, owner Q4).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = invoice domain logic. Content Understanding read, line coding, rules and holds, the transaction and commit gate, tracking and resubmission numbers, reason codes, firm notices and the approval lifecycle stay in `Services/Finance/**`; the harness calls them, it never re-implements or copies them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = eBilling tests. Every existing eBilling unit, integration, ArchTest and end-to-end test passes with no edit to the test files (FR-22 a).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = invariants. "A linked submission is never Failed" and the resume-on-link hold hold under the run record (FR-22 b); `sprk_invoicesubmission` keeps the request role (no `sprk_servicerequest` row for invoices).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">SCOPE = stages. Each stage idempotent with an atomic marker; a resumed run never repeats the Content Understanding read or line coding; the terminal status is written last.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">SCOPE = cutover. Kill switch `Intake:Harnesses:Invoice:Enabled` (default off); off → the existing eBilling path runs exactly as today.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">SCOPE = logs and run records. Ids, statuses and reason codes only; no invoice content.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE = this task's BFF changes. State the Placement Justification in the PR (`.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build (total ≤ 60 MB); no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
