      <pattern name="Scheduled jobs" location=".claude/patterns/api/scheduled-jobs.md">Tag-mapped; not used.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Harness shape" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/Harnesses/Nda/NdaIntakeHarness.cs">Sibling harness from task 015.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">GATE: ask the owner to confirm eBilling UAT sign-off (ebilling-r1 task 163); STOP until confirmed. Then declare RIGOR FULL, tier opus, effort high.</step>
    <step order="2">Run the eBilling suite on the current branch and record the baseline (pass counts) in task notes.</step>
    <step order="3">Read the processing and rerun handlers, note 049 and the NDA harness; write the seam design (which stages, where the run record wraps the existing transaction) in notes/050-invoice-harness-seam.md before coding.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement `InvoiceIntakeHarness` calling the existing Finance services; register it behind the kill switch; touch eBilling handlers only where the seam requires it.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the harness tests; run the full eBilling suite unchanged plus the new tests; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="7">Document deviations in projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Before ANY edit to `Services/Finance/Submission/` or another eBilling file: confirm the eBilling UAT sign-off with the owner; if not signed off, STOP and report.</trigger>
    <trigger>If preserving the invariants needs an existing eBilling test to change, STOP and escalate (FR-22 a) rather than editing the test.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the seam requires changing eBilling's public behaviour or Dataverse schema, STOP and coordinate with ebilling-r1 by message before proceeding.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>spec New Components and notes/reuse-scan.md (invoice row): `InvoiceSubmissionProcessingJobHandler`, `InvoiceSubmissionRerunJobHandler` and `Services/Finance/Submission/*` already do the invoice work; `IIntakeHarness`/`IntakeHarnessRegistry` (task 012) and the NDA harness (015) give the pipeline shape. CAPABILITY-INDEX was checked for an existing invoice orchestrator.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the domain code (called as-is); the new class only adapts it to the harness contract so invoice runs get the run record, DLQ re-drive and status like other requests.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Invoices keep a separate orchestration with its own state, so Phase 3 success criterion 7 fails and the pipeline has one harness, not the general second-harness proof FR-22 requires.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/Harnesses/Invoice/InvoiceIntakeHarness.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/Intake/InvoiceIntakeHarnessTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/050-invoice-harness-seam.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The owner's confirmation of eBilling UAT sign-off is recorded in task notes and precedes the first eBilling-file edit in git history (FR-22 c).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With the switch on, an invoice submission runs as an intake run on `sprk_processingjob` through the existing Finance services; `sprk_invoicesubmission` keeps the request role.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a linked submission is never set Failed; an unlinked submission holds and resumes on link (FR-22 b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a resumed or redelivered run does not repeat the Content Understanding read or line coding.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With the switch off, the existing eBilling path runs unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every existing eBilling test passes with zero diff to its test files; pass counts match the step-2 baseline (FR-22 a).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build and all tests pass; the PR states the Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE). Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative cases named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-22, success criterion 7. The eBilling end-to-end run and dev deploy are task 051. Synthetic invoices only on dev.</notes>

